      "math_academy_id": "e-1071",
      "problem": "Simplify $x\\left(x^3 y^5\\right) \\left(x^2 y^9\\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "Here we have two variables, $x$ and $y.$ We will start by grouping the two variables separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({x}^{3}{y}^{5})({x}^{2}{y}^{9}) & = \\\\ {x}^{1}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{5}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{9} & = \\\\ ({x}^{1}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2})({y}^{5}\\cdot {y}^{9})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis way, we can apply the product rule to the two variables independently:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{1}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2})({y}^{5}\\cdot {y}^{9}) & = \\\\ {x}^{(1+3+2)}\\cdot {y}^{(5+9)} & = \\\\ {x}^{6}{y}^{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
